@giuseppe Thanks for the review and the suggested approach — I've updated the PR to follow it. The change is no longer just removing the close loop; the parent now closes the activation fds only *after* the pause PID race is resolved.
Reproduced the #29964 scenario: a socket-activated `podman.service` racing with the other podman user units that set up the rootless pause process at login. Before the fix, `podman.service` lost its activation fd and failed with `accept4: operation not supported`; with this change it reaches the active state and serves the socket normally.
